WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.766
"A key ablation isolates the role of transfer.

00:00:02.846 --> 00:00:08.087
NeuPL agents are re-initialized either from scratch
or by transferring the encoder and

00:00:08.167 --> 00:00:11.862
memory components of a network trained to epoch one
thousand,

00:00:11.942 --> 00:00:16.069
then tasked with beating fixed Nash mixtures of
increasing strength.

00:00:16.149 --> 00:00:19.101
Against an easily exploitable two-policy mixture,

00:00:19.181 --> 00:00:23.617
even the from-scratch agent eventually finds a
counter, just more slowly.

00:00:23.697 --> 00:00:27.268
But against competent mixtures over four or seven
policies,

00:00:27.348 --> 00:00:31.785
the randomly initialized agent fails outright
despite prolonged training,

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:35.373
while the transferred agent readily discovers the exploit.

00:00:35.453 --> 00:00:39.457
This is NeuPL's most striking property: as the
population expands,

00:00:39.537 --> 00:00:42.860
discovering new strategies becomes easier, not harder."
